.TH "XmeDrawArrow" "library call"
.nh
.SH "NAME"
\fB\%XmeDrawArrow\fP \(em A widget writer function that draws a three-dimensional arrow
.iX "XmeDrawArrow"
.iX "Xme draw functions" "XmeDrawArrow"
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
.nf
#include <Xm/DrawP\&.h>
\fBvoid \fBXmeDrawArrow\fP\fR(
\fBDisplay *\fBdisplay\fR\fR,
\fBDrawable \fBd\fR\fR,
\fBGC \fBtop_gc\fR\fR,
\fBGC \fBbot_gc\fR\fR,
\fBGC \fBcent_gc\fR\fR,
\fBPosition \fBx\fR\fR,
\fBPosition \fBy\fR\fR,
\fBDimension \fBwidth\fR\fR,
\fBDimension \fBheight\fR\fR,
\fBDimension \fBshadow_thick\fR\fR,
\fBunsigned char \fBdirection\fR\fR);
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fB\%XmeDrawArrow\fP draws an arrow, as the ArrowButton does, centered
in
the rectangle \fIx\fP, \fIy\fP, \fIwidth\fP, \fIheight\fP of the
drawable \fId\fP\&.  The
arrow is a square triangle whose side is the smaller of \fIwidth\fP and
\fIheight\fP, less 2 pixels; nothing is drawn if that is less than 1 or
if \fId\fP is None\&.
.PP
The lit edges of the arrow are drawn with \fItop_gc\fP, the dark edges
with
\fIbot_gc\fP and the inside with \fIcent_gc\fP\&.  The shadow is 1 pixel
thick
when \fIshadow_thick\fP is 1 and 2 pixels thick for larger values; with
a
\fIshadow_thick\fP of 0 the whole arrow is filled with \fIcent_gc\fP\&.
If
\fIcent_gc\fP is NULL the inside is not drawn\&.
.IP "\fIdisplay\fP" 10
Specifies the display\&.
.IP "\fId\fP" 10
Specifies the drawable to draw into\&.
.IP "\fItop_gc\fP" 10
Specifies the GC of the lit edges\&.
.IP "\fIbot_gc\fP" 10
Specifies the GC of the dark edges\&.
.IP "\fIcent_gc\fP" 10
Specifies the GC of the inside of the arrow, or NULL\&.
.IP "\fIx\fP" 10
Specifies the x coordinate of the rectangle\&.
.IP "\fIy\fP" 10
Specifies the y coordinate of the rectangle\&.
.IP "\fIwidth\fP" 10
Specifies the width of the rectangle\&.
.IP "\fIheight\fP" 10
Specifies the height of the rectangle\&.
.IP "\fIshadow_thick\fP" 10
Specifies the thickness of the shadow: 0, 1, or 2 and more\&.
.IP "\fIdirection\fP" 10
Specifies where the arrow points: \fB\%XmARROW_UP\fP,
\fB\%XmARROW_DOWN\fP, \fB\%XmARROW_LEFT\fP or \fB\%XmARROW_RIGHT\fP\&.
.PP
Motif 1\&.2 called this function \fB\%_XmDrawArrow\fP\&.  The library
still exports that name for old binaries, and \fB\%<Xm/XmP\&.h>\fP
defines it as a macro for \fB\%XmeDrawArrow\fP unless
\fB\%NO_XM_1_2_BC\fP is defined; new code should use
\fB\%XmeDrawArrow\fP\&.
.SH "RELATED"
.PP
\fB\%XmArrowButton\fP(3) and \fB\%XmeDrawShadows\fP(3)\&.
